ol signals</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>95</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>307</fpage><lpage>318</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9814702</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Oanceaetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oancea</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Teruel</surname><given-names>M.N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Quest</surname><given-names>A.F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Meyer</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Green fluorescent protein (GFP)-tagged cysteine-rich domains from protein kinase C as fluorescent indicators for diacylglycerol signaling in living cells</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol</source><volume>140</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>485</fpage><lpage>498</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9456311</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Pizonetal1994"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pizon</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Desjardins</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Bucci</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Parton</surname><given-names>R.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zerial</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Association of Rap1a and Rap1b proteins with late endocytic/phagocytic compartments and Rap2a with the Golgi complex</article-title><source>J. Cell Sci</source><volume>107</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>1661</fpage><lpage>1670</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7962206</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Raucheretal2000"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Raucher</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stauffer</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Shen</sur